1
00:00:00,858 --> 00:00:02,148
(Penny:)Is that true?

2
00:00:02,318 --> 00:00:05,858
(Leonard:)-It was the only way to make him happy.
-Why'd you have to make him happy?

3
00:00:06,030 --> 00:00:08,820
(Leonard:)Because when he wasn't happy
we wanted to kill him.

4
00:00:10,410 --> 00:00:12,490
That was even a plan.

5
00:00:13,538 --> 00:00:15,708
(Leonard:)We were going to throw
his Kindle outside.

6
00:00:15,873 --> 00:00:20,043
(Leonard:)And when he went to get it, lock
the door and let him freeze to death.

7
00:00:20,378 --> 00:00:22,838
(Sheldon:)-That seems like a bit of an overreaction.
-No.

8
00:00:23,005 --> 00:00:26,555
The overreaction was to tie your limbs
to four different sled-dog teams...

9
00:00:26,717 --> 00:00:28,757
...and yell, "Mush!"

10
00:00:30,680 --> 00:00:34,680
(Leonard:)Look, we kept the original data.
You can still publish the actual results.

11
00:00:34,851 --> 00:00:37,601
(Sheldon:)Yes, but the actual results
are unsuccessful.

12
00:00:37,770 --> 00:00:40,480
I sent an e-mail
to everyone at the university...

13
00:00:40,648 --> 00:00:42,318
...explaining I confirmed
string theory...

14
00:00:42,483 --> 00:00:44,903
(Sheldon:)...and forever changed
man's understanding of the universe.

15
00:00:45,069 --> 00:00:47,489
Oh. See, yeah, you probably
shouldn't have done that.

16
00:00:49,073 --> 00:00:52,283
(Leonard:)So write another e-mail.
Set the record straight. It's no big deal.

17
00:00:54,245 --> 00:00:57,375
(Sheldon:)You're right, Leonard.
That's not a big deal.

18
00:00:57,540 --> 00:01:00,170
(Sheldon:)All you did was lie to me,
destroy my dream...

